# Session 016 (P5 hardening): this file never existed, so `COPY . .` in the
# Dockerfile was copying node_modules/, any local dist/ build output, and —
# critically — the dev-only .env (hardcoded to
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1) straight into the build
# context. Vite loads .env automatically at build time, so the production
# image would have baked in "localhost:8000" as the API host for every
# browser that ever loads it — completely wrong off of localhost. Excluding
# .env here lets the safe fallback in src/services/api.ts
# (`VITE_API_BASE_URL || '/api/v1'`, a same-origin relative path) take over,
# which is exactly what a reverse-proxied production deployment needs.
node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
